1
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,005
(Supported by MCST and KOCCA)

2
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,006
(This drama is purely a work of fiction.)

3
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:08,985
(All scenes with child actors and animals were filmed safely.)

4
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:10,801
Min Seo, what is it?

5
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,637
You hit someone? Hit who?

6
00:00:12,638 --> 00:00:14,555
What are you talking about?

7
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:17,391
Where? Go where?

8
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,684
I don't know.

9
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:21,146
We must hurry up and go, Mom.

10
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:34,785
Ye Ji.

11
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:36,911
It's all right.

12
00:00:36,912 --> 00:00:38,038
Don't worry.

13
00:00:38,622 --> 00:00:39,915
It's okay.

14
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:42,626
It's all right.

15
00:00:50,926 --> 00:00:52,719
(A few months before the accident)

16
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,556
Min Seo.

17
00:00:56,557 --> 00:01:00,309
Are you sure you don't want a ride?

18
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,186
- Hello. - Good morning.

19
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:03,688
We just moved here.

20
00:01:03,689 --> 00:01:05,231
- Hi. - Wait.

21
00:01:05,232 --> 00:01:07,525
- Do you go to Cheongnam Girls' Middle School too? - Hi.

22
00:01:07,526 --> 00:01:08,610
This is great.

23
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:10,736
We were just heading out to drop our daughter off at school.

24
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:12,029
Would you like a ride?

25
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:15,366
It's a great way to save time and gas in a country with no oil,

26
00:01:15,367 --> 00:01:17,493
plus the girls can quickly become friends.

27
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:19,579
Neighbors should help each other out.

28
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:22,665
Right, but not now.

29
00:01:22,666 --> 00:01:25,042
Or what do you say...

30
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:26,670
to having dinner together this weekend?

31
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,381
Make time for us with your husband.

32
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:32,217
Oh, I'm quite good at cooking too.

33
00:01:32,718 --> 00:01:33,719
I see.

34
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:38,557
I didn't expect someone as famous as you to move in right across the road.

35
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:42,519
Indeed. We never thought we'd end up in this neighborhood either.

36
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:45,022
It's all thanks to Captain Park right here.

37
00:01:45,856 --> 00:01:48,024
I know you film in different neighborhoods.

38
00:01:48,025 --> 00:01:50,610
You aren't planning to shoot here, are you?

39
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:53,947
You see, I'm not used to such a disturbance.

40
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:57,658
I stopped by to drop this off yesterday, but you weren't home.

41
00:01:57,659 --> 00:01:58,702
It's a moving-in gift.

42
00:01:59,161 --> 00:02:01,401
You really don't have to go out of your way from now on.

43
00:02:02,873 --> 00:02:04,207
Not at all.

44
00:02:05,292 --> 00:02:08,128
Too much kindness can feel a bit overwhelming.

45
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:13,382
Min Seo, get in.

46
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:15,135
Thank you for the ride.

47
00:02:20,432 --> 00:02:22,684
What the heck? This is insane.

48
00:02:32,194 --> 00:02:33,779
(Galaxy Express)

49
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:40,202
Wait.

50
00:02:41,036 --> 00:02:42,829
I like that song too.

51
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:47,333
("Bye Bye Planet")

52
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:48,960
All right, let's head to school.

53
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:56,634
What's this?

54
00:02:56,635 --> 00:02:57,844
What is this song?

55
00:02:59,471 --> 00:03:00,806
You listen to stuff like this?

56
00:03:01,098 --> 00:03:04,059
What are you saying? I've always liked this stuff.

57
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:32,753
Oh, my gosh, what if we get caught?

58
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,840
Don't worry, and just trust me.

59
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,554
I see.

60
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:44,098
So, your actual name is Lim Jae Hong?

61
00:03:44,099 --> 00:03:45,141
Tacky, isn't it?

62
00:03:45,142 --> 00:03:46,851
At home, my wife always calls me,

63
00:03:46,852 --> 00:03:49,103
"Hong!"

64
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:50,104
All the time.

65
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:51,439
Like a pet name.

66
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,816
It is a pet name.

67
00:03:53,442 --> 00:03:56,819
It makes perfect sense now why you share such an intimate bond.

68
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:57,863
There's a running...

69
00:03:58,363 --> 00:04:00,865
What now? Want me to go grab an opener?

70
00:04:00,866 --> 00:04:03,284
No need. I'm almost done.

71
00:04:03,285 --> 00:04:05,745
Come on and put some muscle into it.

72
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:07,079
I can do it.

73
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,331
No, you can't.

74
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:10,459
Yes, I can.

75
00:04:13,003 --> 00:04:14,086
Oh, my.

76
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:15,921
- See? I told you. - Awesome.

77
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,424
Seriously.

78
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:20,886
Do you want to take a look at this?

79
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:23,095
What is this?

80
00:04:23,096 --> 00:04:25,849
Just look at the front pages. The back is not done yet.

81
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:28,643
You drew all these?

82
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,604
Oh, my.

83
00:04:31,062 --> 00:04:33,023
I thought they were pictures.

84
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:36,026
I didn't know you were this good.

85
00:04:36,568 --> 00:04:38,612
You're like a total art genius.

86
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:40,822
It's incredible.

87
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:43,074
Did you design this?

88
00:04:44,576 --> 00:04:46,535
Hey, I told you not to look at the back.

89
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:48,329
It's a million times better...

90
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:50,247
than my dad's ugly dung-colored car.

91
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:51,248
Awesome.

92
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:54,711
You should just start your own car company.

93
00:04:55,212 --> 00:04:57,839
My mom hates me drawing.

94
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:01,301
My dad tells me to do what I want.

95
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,846
But if my mom were for it,

96
00:05:05,347 --> 00:05:07,182
he would be against it.

97
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:11,478
They don't give a thing about what I actually want.

98
00:05:12,062 --> 00:05:14,105
They just use me to fight each other.

99
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:19,820
So honestly, I was glad when they announced the divorce.

100
00:05:20,362 --> 00:05:22,113
They fought every single day,

101
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:24,658
always screaming and swearing.

102
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:26,993
When they did,

103
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:30,205
I'd hide in the car and play loud music.

104
00:05:31,081 --> 00:05:32,415
It helped a bit.

105
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,670
You're lucky your parents are on good terms.

106
00:05:41,842 --> 00:05:43,009
I will...

107
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:45,846
take you for a drive someday later.

108
00:05:47,806 --> 00:05:49,348
Come on,

109
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:53,687
we'll blast that loud music you like...

110
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:57,190
and hit 200 kilometers...

111
00:05:57,691 --> 00:05:59,109
an hour.

112
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:02,403
Why are you laughing?

113
00:06:02,404 --> 00:06:03,822
I'm being serious.

114
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:06,741
I get driving lessons from my dad sometimes.

115
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:09,035
I'm really good at it.

116
00:06:59,711 --> 00:07:01,254
I think moving here was a good idea.

117
00:07:02,047 --> 00:07:03,173
Right?

118
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:06,635
Right.

119
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:16,102
(Memories just between us)

120
00:07:31,910 --> 00:07:32,994
(Min Seo)

121
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:39,334
(Save)

122
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:44,714
(Matching rings)

123
00:07:56,518 --> 00:07:58,227
What's going on?

124
00:07:58,228 --> 00:07:59,813
No idea.

125
00:08:07,529 --> 00:08:10,281
(Dialing)

126
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,705
Min Seo,

127
00:08:17,706 --> 00:08:18,707
are you okay?

128
00:08:19,916 --> 00:08:21,250
I'm all right.

129
00:08:21,251 --> 00:08:22,835
Min Seo.

130
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:26,089
Can you come out and talk to me for a second?

131
00:08:28,425 --> 00:08:30,759
Why don't we go for a drive?

132
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,970
A drive?

133
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:34,139
Like we said the other day,

134
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:36,850
we'll blast some loud music...

135
00:08:38,309 --> 00:08:40,103
and just drive super fast.

136
00:09:02,751 --> 00:09:06,046
Both my parents are getting back late today.

137
00:09:09,591 --> 00:09:11,884
Ye Ji, are you chickening out?

138
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:13,136
No, I'm not.

139
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,304
I told you.

140
00:09:15,305 --> 00:09:17,431
My dad taught me how to drive. I'm really good.

141
00:09:17,432 --> 00:09:18,682
As if.

142
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,310
Are you sure you can do it?

143
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:21,936
Of course.

144
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:26,982
So where are we going?

145
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,026
What?

146
00:09:33,907 --> 00:09:35,825
Is there anywhere you want to go?

147
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:38,953
Just...

148
00:09:40,538 --> 00:09:42,332
somewhere secluded.

149
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:46,419
Oh, right.

150
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:47,879
Hang on.

151
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,216
Search for somewhere quiet and secluded.

152
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,384
Hey, that's not going to work.

153
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,385
A quiet and secluded place...

154
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:57,471
in your recent destinations.

155
00:09:57,472 --> 00:09:58,764
Would you like directions?

156
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:00,767
- See? It works. - What the heck?

157
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:06,230
Starting route to "a quiet and secluded place."

158
00:10:06,231 --> 00:10:12,237
(The Affair Was Just The Beginning)

159
00:10:14,781 --> 00:10:19,536
(Episode 3: A Quiet And Secluded Place)

160
00:11:05,123 --> 00:11:06,541
I can't believe this.

161
00:11:08,418 --> 00:11:09,793
What on earth happened?

162
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:10,919
Ye Ji.

163
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,713
What's with my car?

164
00:11:12,714 --> 00:11:14,131
Did you not hear anything?

165
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:15,300
Dad...

166
00:11:19,888 --> 00:11:21,681
What do I do?

167
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:08,019
He's too heavy.

168
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,188
No.

169
00:12:10,772 --> 00:12:12,190
This is for my daughter, Ye Ji.

170
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:15,443
I'm sorry.

171
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:36,297
Oh, gosh.

172
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,050
Jeez, it's killing me.

173
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:49,138
I didn't know you had a thing for places like these.

174
00:12:58,111 --> 00:12:59,320
I'm sorry.

175
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:03,031
It wasn't intentional.

176
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,367
Oh, goodness.

177
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:12,417
Wait.

178
00:13:16,838 --> 00:13:17,839
Honey.

179
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:20,424
Honey!

180
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:21,467
Sweetie.

181
00:13:22,677 --> 00:13:24,261
Honey, it's me.

182
00:13:24,262 --> 00:13:25,679
It's me.

183
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:26,973
It's me, Hong.

184
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:29,182
- Lim Jae Hong? - Yes.

185
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:30,184
You...

186
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:33,021
What are you doing in that mess?

187
00:13:33,604 --> 00:13:34,689
Shush.

188
00:13:37,692 --> 00:13:38,818
What on earth?

189
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:41,696
I thought you came after hearing from Ye Ji.

190
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:43,489
Ye Ji?

191
00:13:44,324 --> 00:13:45,742
What about her?

192
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:48,161
Hear what from her?

193
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,621
Apparently...

194
00:13:54,042 --> 00:13:55,710
Our daughter...

195
00:13:56,794 --> 00:13:58,129
hit someone.

196
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:03,342
This brat took my car...

197
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:06,554
without asking and got into a wreck.

198
00:14:15,772 --> 00:14:16,814
Darn it.

199
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,410
Stay here.

200
00:14:34,207 --> 00:14:35,208
Wait.

201
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:44,383
- Hello? - Hello, Attorney Cho.

202
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:46,385
I'm so sorry for calling late at night.

203
00:14:46,386 --> 00:14:47,469
No problem.

204
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:48,804
- I'm calling because... - Go on.

205
00:14:48,805 --> 00:14:49,889
Because...

206
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,015
Well...

207
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:55,352
My daughter, Min Seo, has a classmate...

208
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:58,814
whose parent's acquaintance's daughter...

209
00:14:58,815 --> 00:15:00,273
I mean, son.

210
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:03,026
I see. That's quite a close connection.

211
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:05,530
Yes, incredibly close.

212
00:15:06,364 --> 00:15:09,992
Anyway, it seems the son took a car out...

213
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,994
and hit someone.

214
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:16,331
He was so terrified that he just came straight home,

215
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:17,916
and I'd like...

216
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:20,001
to know what happens...

217
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:22,337
if he turns...

218
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:24,841
himself in.

219
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:27,551
How's the victim?

220
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:29,094
The sentence changes a lot...

221
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:31,054
depending on whether it's an injury or death...

222
00:15:31,055 --> 00:15:32,639
and how bad the injury is.

223
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:35,058
Make sure the victim gets medical help first.

224
00:15:35,059 --> 00:15:36,518
Okay.

225
00:15:36,519 --> 00:15:38,061
Then, let me...

226
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:40,063
assess the situation first...

227
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,440
and get back to you.

228
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:43,358
Dr. Ahn. Just in case...

229
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:46,027
- I'm telling you just in case. - Yes?

230
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:47,946
This is purely hypothetical.

231
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:50,949
But if Min Seo's friend's parent's acquaintance...

232
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:54,077
happens to be in a custody battle like you...

233
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:56,246
Custody?

234
00:15:56,247 --> 00:15:59,958
Yes, they absolutely need legal advice to avoid losing custody.

235
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,793
One wrong move and the court could see them...

236
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:03,462
as a parent who can't manage their child.

237
00:16:03,463 --> 00:16:06,883
That's really bad for a custody case.

238
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:16,267
(Ye Ji)

239
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,603
Just quietly listen to what she says.

240
00:16:19,604 --> 00:16:21,230
She may be recording the call.

241
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:27,195
Hi, Ye Ji.

242
00:16:29,322 --> 00:16:30,573
Min Seo.

243
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:32,908
I'm sorry.

244
00:16:32,909 --> 00:16:34,285
I shouldn't have...

245
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:36,746
Because of me...

246
00:16:42,919 --> 00:16:44,085
Oh, his arm must hurt.

247
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:46,755
No, tell me this isn't true.

248
00:16:46,756 --> 00:16:48,382
- It can't be. No... - Goodness.

249
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:51,009
- What do we... - I'm sorry.

250
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,845
Babe, it's not too late to take him to the hospital.

251
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:56,098
- Maybe he's still... - It's too late.

252
00:16:56,933 --> 00:16:58,351
I already checked.

253
00:17:03,105 --> 00:17:05,399
There's no way Ye Ji would do this.

254
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:07,401
Oh, my goodness.

255
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,405
Darn it.

256
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:17,411
Wait. Don't tell me you...

257
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:21,541
Are you out of your mind? What are you trying to do?

258
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:25,211
What was I supposed to do, then?

259
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,671
Ye Ji was sobbing frantically...

260
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:29,715
about the crash she caused.

261
00:17:30,341 --> 00:17:32,802
I rushed here in a panic,

262
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:35,637
and that guy was...

263
00:17:35,638 --> 00:17:37,055
already dead.

264
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:38,848
But I couldn't possibly...

265
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:40,685
turn in my own daughter.

266
00:17:43,813 --> 00:17:45,272
Why did you move him here?

267
00:17:45,273 --> 00:17:48,150
What if someone walks by and sees it out here?

268
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:52,404
Moving him here doesn't just undo this.

269
00:17:52,405 --> 00:17:53,738
This can't be hidden!

270
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:55,615
I had to do something.

271
00:17:55,616 --> 00:17:56,951
I'm her dad, you know.

272
00:18:00,705 --> 00:18:01,747
Goodness, gracious.

273
00:18:20,266 --> 00:18:21,267
Let's turn her in.

274
00:18:23,394 --> 00:18:25,812
If we hire a skilled lawyer and turn her in,

275
00:18:25,813 --> 00:18:27,231
- then... - Oh, my gosh.

276
00:18:27,732 --> 00:18:28,941
Jeez, that startled me.

277
00:18:32,278 --> 00:18:33,862
Turn her in?

278
00:18:33,863 --> 00:18:35,740
Would that be better?

279
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:38,326
Sorry.

280
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:40,703
I need to take this call.

281
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:46,125
Hello, Mr. Ha. What brings you...

282
00:18:47,001 --> 00:18:48,543
Goodness.

283
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:50,378
Chairwoman Jeong wants to meet me...

284
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:51,631
tomorrow?

285
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,842
Yes, I can make time.

286
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:57,761
(Missed Calls)

287
00:18:57,762 --> 00:18:58,929
False rumors?

288
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:00,180
(Min Seo's Mother, CEO Kim)

289
00:19:00,181 --> 00:19:01,640
Articles...

290
00:19:01,641 --> 00:19:03,808
Oh, right.

291
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:05,394
Crazy things do happen after all.

292
00:19:05,645 --> 00:19:07,563
(CEO Kim)

293
00:19:09,982 --> 00:19:11,650
No, I fully understand. Of course.

294
00:19:11,651 --> 00:19:13,778
(The scriptwriter wants you as the next male lead.)

295
00:19:14,737 --> 00:19:16,322
Yes, I know that place.

296
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:19,325
Yes, I'll see you at lunch tomorrow.

297
00:19:24,664 --> 00:19:26,039
Articles are out saying...

298
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,042
Ryu Ji Su is having an affair with Kang Tae Han.

299
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:30,919
See? I told you.

300
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:33,297
It really wasn't me and Ryu Ji Su.

301
00:19:35,341 --> 00:19:36,550
Indeed.

302
00:19:39,345 --> 00:19:41,347
At least, one problem is solved.

303
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:48,020
Seriously, what do we do about this?

304
00:19:50,981 --> 00:19:52,066
Gosh, my back.

305
00:20:04,245 --> 00:20:06,205
We should look for a lawyer first, right?

306
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:09,874
Right.

307
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:11,585
I guess we have to.

308
00:20:16,048 --> 00:20:17,383
Let's go home.

309
00:20:18,384 --> 00:20:20,135
Let's go home...

310
00:20:20,136 --> 00:20:21,762
- Right. - and talk to Ye Ji first.

311
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,977
This will be all over the Internet.

312
00:20:28,853 --> 00:20:30,270
I know.

313
00:20:30,271 --> 00:20:33,606
Once it's out, it stays permanent these days.

314
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,692
It will follow her like a shadow,

315
00:20:35,693 --> 00:20:37,444
no matter what she tries to do.

316
00:20:37,445 --> 00:20:40,239
Exactly. And people never let these things go.

317
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:43,575
Can Ye Ji even handle this?

318
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:46,453
She's easily influenced by her surroundings.

319
00:20:46,454 --> 00:20:48,581
She's already so fragile...

320
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:51,083
I mean,

321
00:20:52,001 --> 00:20:55,378
Ye Ji isn't the type to do something like this on purpose.

322
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:57,255
It was an accident.

323
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:58,506
Right.

324
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:00,301
What if she goes to juvy,

325
00:21:00,843 --> 00:21:03,011
meets the wrong crowd,

326
00:21:03,012 --> 00:21:05,306
and goes completely off the rails?

327
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:18,068
Maybe it's better...

328
00:21:19,779 --> 00:21:21,864
if we just teach her...

329
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:25,117
so she never makes a mistake like this again.

330
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:27,453
Exactly.

331
00:21:28,954 --> 00:21:30,790
At the end of the day, we're her parents.

332
00:21:32,625 --> 00:21:33,792
My gosh.

333
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:35,795
Darn, that startled me.

334
00:22:07,618 --> 00:22:09,161
(Dr. Joo)

335
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:13,499
(Power off)

336
00:22:19,505 --> 00:22:21,298
- Honey. - What?

337
00:22:21,841 --> 00:22:24,342
There are no security cameras around here,

338
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:26,136
and no one lives in this area.

339
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:32,726
You know this neighborhood?

340
00:22:34,228 --> 00:22:35,229
What?

341
00:22:36,897 --> 00:22:39,358
It's known as a shantytown.

342
00:22:40,150 --> 00:22:43,529
There's a mountain straight up behind here.

343
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:47,282
If we quietly bury him there...

344
00:22:47,283 --> 00:22:48,491
No.

345
00:22:48,492 --> 00:22:50,077
No, that's a no.

346
00:22:50,494 --> 00:22:51,494
Do you have...

347
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:53,372
- a better idea? - Stay there and talk.

348
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:58,252
If this gets out, it's over for us too...

349
00:22:59,086 --> 00:23:00,588
Keep your distance.

350
00:23:01,297 --> 00:23:02,964
I'm saying...

351
00:23:02,965 --> 00:23:04,674
we're Ye Ji's parents.

352
00:23:04,675 --> 00:23:07,386
We have to protect her.

353
00:23:08,846 --> 00:23:09,847
Honey.

354
00:23:10,681 --> 00:23:12,016
I'm great at shoveling.

355
00:23:12,892 --> 00:23:14,977
You know how much I shoveled back in the army?

356
00:23:16,353 --> 00:23:18,354
Didn't you see the banners when you drove in?

357
00:23:18,355 --> 00:23:19,856
(Public Redevelopment Project)

358
00:23:19,857 --> 00:23:21,275
(Redevelopment Project Confirmed)

359
00:23:25,613 --> 00:23:29,157
My dad went to the crash site,

360
00:23:29,158 --> 00:23:31,034
so I'll ask him when he gets back.

361
00:23:31,035 --> 00:23:32,703
Okay, Ye Ji.

362
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,248
Min Seo.

363
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:39,000
Don't ever tell your mom...

364
00:23:39,001 --> 00:23:40,961
about us, okay?

365
00:23:48,594 --> 00:23:49,969
(Contacts)

366
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,180
(Dialing)

367
00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:01,899
The number cannot be reached. You'll be directed to voicemail...

368
00:24:07,488 --> 00:24:13,160
(Is something wrong?)

369
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:33,221
Why didn't you answer my calls? I was worried.

370
00:24:33,222 --> 00:24:34,639
Sorry.

371
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:35,641
Wait.

372
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:37,977
Ye Ji.

373
00:24:38,978 --> 00:24:40,312
I think...

374
00:24:41,855 --> 00:24:44,692
we need to delete the dashcam footage.

375
00:24:45,359 --> 00:24:47,276
Where is your mom going?

376
00:24:47,277 --> 00:24:48,320
What?

377
00:24:49,947 --> 00:24:52,074
Well...

378
00:24:53,242 --> 00:24:54,368
The thing is...

379
00:25:02,543 --> 00:25:04,086
Why did you go there?

380
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:09,717
How did you even know that place?

381
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:12,678
I don't know.

382
00:25:13,554 --> 00:25:14,887
We just...

383
00:25:14,888 --> 00:25:16,849
followed the navigation history in Mr. Lim's car.

384
00:25:21,437 --> 00:25:23,022
That car's navigation history...

385
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:48,439
The number cannot...

386
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:50,317
Why aren't any of them picking up?

387
00:26:51,401 --> 00:26:52,945
I'm sorry, Ye Ji.

388
00:26:55,739 --> 00:26:56,990
Where are you going?

389
00:26:57,407 --> 00:26:59,034
To my parents!

390
00:27:04,706 --> 00:27:07,417
Your mom's obviously going to blow the whole thing.

391
00:27:09,128 --> 00:27:10,921
Was I asking for too much?

392
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:13,507
I just asked you to trust me...

393
00:27:14,091 --> 00:27:16,301
and stay quiet.

394
00:27:17,136 --> 00:27:19,304
Why couldn't you even do that one thing?

395
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:22,266
Meanwhile, I had to tell those lies for you.

396
00:27:22,933 --> 00:27:25,144
I never asked you to lie for me.

397
00:27:32,985 --> 00:27:34,152
Hey.

398
00:27:34,153 --> 00:27:36,363
You were the one...

399
00:27:36,947 --> 00:27:39,283
You made all the choices. What was I supposed to do?

400
00:27:46,290 --> 00:27:47,540
I made all the choices?

401
00:27:47,541 --> 00:27:49,209
Yes, you did.

402
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:52,129
You regret hiding me, don't you?

403
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:56,382
Go tell your dad everything. Tell him you're innocent.

404
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:58,050
That I was the one who hit him, not you.

405
00:27:58,051 --> 00:27:59,260
Tell him!

406
00:27:59,261 --> 00:28:01,012
I'll just go to prison.

407
00:28:01,013 --> 00:28:02,431
Isn't that what you want?

408
00:28:24,036 --> 00:28:25,078
My gosh.

409
00:28:51,146 --> 00:28:53,023
I didn't see him.

410
00:28:53,774 --> 00:28:55,233
I swear...

411
00:28:55,234 --> 00:28:56,777
I had no idea he was there.

412
00:28:58,654 --> 00:28:59,737
Let's go.

413
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,656
Let's go right now and tell the truth.

414
00:29:01,657 --> 00:29:03,366
- I didn't see him. - I'll handle it.

415
00:29:03,367 --> 00:29:04,618
- Get in. - He suddenly...

416
00:29:30,936 --> 00:29:32,437
Jeez.

417
00:30:17,524 --> 00:30:19,151
If we can't wipe it, we'll cover it up.

418
00:30:37,544 --> 00:30:40,379
Min Seo, where are you kids going?

419
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:44,259
- Are you perhaps... - Did you meet my parents?

420
00:30:45,135 --> 00:30:46,469
Well,

421
00:30:46,470 --> 00:30:48,597
I went there, and...

422
00:30:50,098 --> 00:30:51,808
